Optimized Matching Algorithm
function matchRider(request):

    location = request.location

    candidates = spatialIndex.search(
        location,
        SEARCH_RADIUS
    )

    available = filter(
        candidates,
        driver.status == AVAILABLE
    )

    ranked = sortBy(
        available,
        distance + estimatedArrivalTime
    )

    for driver in ranked:

        if reserve(driver):
            return driver

    return NO_DRIVER_AVAILABLE
Complexity

If there are N total drivers, a naive approach may examine:

O(N)

drivers for every request.

With a spatial index, the search is focused on nearby drivers, giving substantially lower practical search cost, approximately:

O(log N + K)

where K is the number of nearby candidates returned by the index.

